  "Question": "Six numbers from a list of nine integers are \\(7,\\) \\(8,\\) \\(3,\\) \\(5,\\) \\(9,\\) and \\(5.\\) The largest possible value of the median of all nine numbers in this list is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(5\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(7\\)",
    "D": "\\(8\\)",
    "E": "\\(9\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "When nine numbers are arranged from smallest to largest, their median is the fifth number. Among the given entries, the five numbers \\(3,5,5,7,8\\) are all at most \\(8\\). Thus, regardless of the three missing numbers, the fifth number cannot exceed \\(8\\).\n\nThis bound can be reached. Choose the missing integers to be \\(10,11,12\\). The complete sorted list is\n\\[\n3,5,5,7,8,9,10,11,12,\n\\]\nand its fifth number is \\(8\\). Therefore the largest possible median is \\(8\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
